[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Real per-namespace RBAC, PodSecurity restricted, etcd secret encryption -- majority of mapped controls" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC6" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/platform-console/k8s/rbac.yaml, /Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/platform-console/k8s/services-and-deployments.yaml:171,481,586,694,850, /Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md" ;
    dcterms:description "rbac.yaml grants least-privilege get/list/watch Roles scoped per tenant namespace plus one narrowly-scoped ClusterRole (get+create only on namespaces) for resolve_tenant_namespace() in services/ggen/app.py:215; services-and-deployments.yaml sets securityContext with seccompProfile RuntimeDefault at multiple deployment blocks; SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md items #1 and #3 document real, live-verified etcd secret encryption and PodSecurity restricted-profile admission enforcement with real negative/positive kubectl tests. This is the largest mapped TSC category (CC6, 15+ rows in SOC2-CONTROL-MAPPING.md) but per-control automated regression tests were not found -- verification was manual/one-time kubectl proof, so IMPLEMENTED not TESTED for most rows; the RBAC ClusterRole gap the task description flagged as a historical open item appears already closed in this checkout (a scoped ClusterRole exists, comment explains why cluster scope was needed). Note: an mTLS claim originally in this finding's label was not substantiated by the cited evidence (only a passing comment in rbac.yaml, no mTLS config in the cited files; Istio sidecar injection is explicitly disabled for several deployments) and has been dropped." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Tamper-evident hash-chained audit log, live-verified once, no automated test found" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC7" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md (item 4, audit-db.ts)" ;
    dcterms:description "app/lib/audit-db.ts chains audit_log rows via SHA-256 (row_hash = sha256(prev_hash+fields)) under a pg_advisory_xact_lock, with verifyAuditChain() and a real demonstrated tamper-detection test performed manually against a live Postgres pod (UPDATE via kubectl exec+psql broke the chain, verify returned brokenAt; row restored, chain valid again). This is real, working code with a real one-time proof, but no automated *.test.ts exercises it (searched, none found), so status is IMPLEMENTED, not TESTED." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "CI admission gates (crown.yml) and k8s ValidatingAdmissionPolicy enforce change management" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC8" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/.github/workflows/crown.yml:22-44,65-81, /Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/scripts/crown.sh:1-51" ;
    dcterms:description "crown.yml's 'fast' job runs cargo fmt/clippy plus catalog/architecture/projection validation on every push/PR to main; its 'test' job runs cargo test --workspace; scripts/crown.sh additionally produces and self-verifies a signed build manifest (sha256 of Cargo.lock and the built binary, cross-checked with jq/test assertions) before Crown standing can advance. SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md item 2 also documents a live ValidatingAdmissionPolicy that blocks deployments referencing CVE-denylisted images. These are real CI gate definitions confirmed present and well-formed; status is IMPLEMENTED rather than TESTED because no independent access to a currently-passing GitHub Actions run log or live cluster session was available to confirm the gates are currently/recently passing in production." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Single-node cluster risk explicitly disclosed as an unmitigated availability/operational risk, not a formal risk-mitigation program" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC9-1" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md (Still Open, IaaS section)" ;
