[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Availability commitments (capacity planning against commitments)" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "NOT-STARTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/platform-console/docs/SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md:98-103 (section 4, 'No real customer-facing SLA')" ;
    dcterms:description "The repo explicitly and repeatedly disclaims any contractual availability commitment: /status computes a real Prometheus-derived uptime% (avg_over_time(up{component=\"...\"}[1h]) in app/lib/status-page.ts:114-116) but SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md states in its own words 'What it is not: an SLA... this page reports uptime observed from this single-node cluster; it makes no promise about future uptime, offers no remedy for downtime, and has no counterparty.' No SLA document, uptime target, or capacity-commitment doc exists anywhere in the repo. There is real capacity monitoring (see A1-2) but no documented availability commitment for that monitoring to be measured against." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Environmental protection / backup / capacity monitoring" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/platform-console/k8s/hpa.yaml; k8s/resource-quotas.yaml; k8s/status-page.yaml; app/lib/k8s.ts:1604 createBackupJob" ;
    dcterms:description "Real, live-cluster HorizontalPodAutoscalers (k8s/hpa.yaml, CPU-utilization target 70%, real min/max replica bounds cross-checked against ResourceQuota headroom per that file's own comment), real per-namespace ResourceQuota objects (k8s/resource-quotas.yaml, sized from an observed Istio-sidecar-inclusive per-pod cost, not guessed), a real Prometheus-scraped platform-prober Deployment (k8s/status-page.yaml) performing genuine HTTP/TCP checks against 8 components every scrape, and a real on-demand Postgres backup mechanism (app/lib/k8s.ts createBackupJob, a real batch/v1 Job running pg_dump against a live-resolved Postgres Pod, wired through app/app/api/projects/[name]/backups/route.ts and app/components/RunBackupButton.tsx). No CronJob-based scheduled backup was found as a default (SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md notes backups are on-demand 'or via a CronJob, if scheduled through /scheduled-jobs'). No test file exercises the HPA or capacity-quota behavior itself (only the backup path has an e2e test, credited to A1-3)." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Tested recovery procedures" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-3" ;
    dcterms:type "TESTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "/Users/sac/chatman-ecosystem/platform-console/docs/DISASTER-RECOVERY.md; app/e2e/core-paas.spec.ts:143-169" ;
    dcterms:description "docs/DISASTER-RECOVERY.md documents a real disaster that already happened (unrecoverable etcd bbolt-checksum panic, cited to infra/kind-config.yaml's committed header and a specific git commit hash/timestamp) and a real, live-executed recovery-primitive proof performed while writing the doc: a real ConfigMap was captured via kubectl get -o yaml, backed up to evidence/dr-proof/platform-feature-flags-backup.yaml, deleted, confirmed broken via both kubectl and a live authenticated curl against the running app, then restored via kubectl apply and confirmed byte-identical to the pre-deletion state at both the k8s and app layer (transcripts inline in the doc). Separately, app/e2e/core-paas.spec.ts:143-169 is a real Playwright test that loads /projects/autofde-lab/backups and asserts on real backup-job table/status-badge state (not a mock). The evidence-bundle entry 'backup-job-verified-nonempty' documents a real end-to-end backup-job run (POST /api/backups -> 201, polled Job reaching status.succeeded=1) through the live deployed pod." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Data classification policy/scheme" ;
