[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Protection mechanisms for data in transit and secrets at rest" ;
    dcterms:subject "C1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "platform-console/k8s/mtls.yaml; platform-console/k8s/mtls-gateway.yaml; platform-console/services/ggen/app.py:252-270; platform-console/app/lib/k8s.ts (per evidence bundle control #11); platform-console/k8s/paas-rbac.yaml (per evidence bundle control #12)" ;
    dcterms:description "Real, on-disk evidence of multiple protection mechanisms: (1) k8s/mtls.yaml defines Istio PeerAuthentication objects in STRICT mode for 5 namespaces (autofde-lab, gymact, ggen, ggen-marketplace, platform-console), enforcing service-to-service mTLS; (2) k8s/mtls-gateway.yaml adds a second Istio Gateway on port 8444 requiring client-cert mutual TLS (tls.mode: MUTUAL) scoped narrowly to the destructive /api/projects/*/backups route, with the CA private key deliberately kept out of the cluster and out of the repo; (3) services/ggen/app.py:252-270 (resolve_signing_key()) implements protection for a receipt-signing key: prefers an operator-injected GGEN_SIGNING_KEY env var, falls back to a locally generated 32-byte hex key written with 0o600 permissions; (4) per platform-console/evidence/control-evidence-bundle.json controls #11 (secrets-never-logged-or-rendered) and #12 (least-privilege-per-namespace-secrets-rbac, k8s/paas-rbac.yaml Roles limited to get,list,create,delete on secrets, no patch/update/watch). A Playwright e2e test (app/e2e/security-observability.spec.ts, 'never renders a raw secret value') covers the secrets-rendering UI slice, but mTLS enforcement, RBAC verb restrictions, and mtls-gateway routing remain verified only via narrated live kubectl/HTTP re-verification, not repo-resident automated tests, so status is IMPLEMENTED rather than TESTED." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Inputs are complete, accurate, timely, and authorized before processing" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "platform-console/services/ggen/ggen-src/crates/ggen-graph/src/interchangeable.rs:53-75 (admit_input); crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs:1343-1370 (evaluate_gate); crates/ggen-graph/src/bin/sparql_gate_check.rs:131-178" ;
    dcterms:description "A SPARQL/N-Quad 'outer membrane' rejects empty input and known injection patterns (DROP GRAPH/DELETE WHERE) before admission; ggen-engine's evaluate_gate() runs SPARQL ASK/SELECT admission gates fail-closed against pack-supplied RDF before generation proceeds, and sparql_gate_check.rs is a real binary that executes each pack's .rq gate against the composed graph and reports PASS/FAIL. The admission/gate control code is real and matches its description, but the test originally cited as TESTED evidence (verify_pack_gate_sabotage_e2e.rs, output_count_regression_gate_refuses_a_real_output_shrink) currently fails in this checkout with a hard missing-fixture error (read_dir: No such file or directory -- the ggen-verify-pack fixture pack the test depends on is absent), so status is IMPLEMENTED, not TESTED." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "System processes data completely, accurately, timely to meet objectives (edit checks, error handling)" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "TESTED" ;
