    dcterms:source "platform-console/services/ggen/ggen-src/crates/praxis-core/src/receipt_validator.rs:287-334 (ReceiptValidator::validate, tests lawful_chain_passes_every_stage); crates/praxis-core/src/verify.rs:524-563 (run_pipeline_accepts_a_lawful_chain)" ;
    dcterms:description "A multi-stage validator (schema/chain/andon/etc.) runs over ReceiptRecord sequences produced during processing and is exercised by real passing unit tests asserting the verdict and per-stage outcomes on constructed chained records (cargo test -p praxis-core --lib lawful_chain_passes_every_stage: 1 passed, 0 failed); SPARQL gates (evaluate_gate, ggen-engine/src/sync.rs) fail-closed mid-pipeline when a pack's own invariant is violated, also covered by real e2e tests (verify_pack_gate_sabotage_e2e.rs)." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "System produces complete, accurate, timely output; distributed to intended parties" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-3" ;
    dcterms:type "TESTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "platform-console/services/ggen/ggen-src/crates/ggen-engine/tests/projection_determinism_test.rs:46-99; tests/multi_template_determinism.rs:96-141; tests/cli_boundary.rs:202-270" ;
    dcterms:description "Real passing tests assert that two independent fresh syncs of identical fixtures produce byte-identical output trees and identical graph_hash/receipt payload bytes, and that a second run of the same project reproduces the same output and reports 'unchanged: content identical' via ggen sync run --dry-run -- output completeness/accuracy is asserted on real files on disk, not mocked (cargo test -p ggen-engine --test projection_determinism_test --test multi_template_determinism --test cli_boundary: 28/28, 3/3, 3/3 passed). 'Distributed to intended parties' has no evidence located (no delivery/notification-integrity control found) -- output-correctness half only." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "System maintains complete, accurate, timely records of system inputs" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-4" ;
    dcterms:type "IMPLEMENTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "platform-console/services/ggen/ggen-src/crates/praxis-core/src/receipt_record.rs:1-90; platform-console/services/autofde-lab-mcp/src/autofde_lab/hub/domain/gym_procedure/level4_ocel.py:1348-1523 (build_level4_ocel)" ;
    dcterms:description "ReceiptRecord carries payload_hash_hex (BLAKE3 of canonical JSON input), instruction_id, ts_ns and an origin/provenance tag distinguishing unattended-dispatch writes from reviewed ones; level4_ocel.py projects receipts into a real OCEL v2 log with AuthorityAdmitted/ActuationOpened/ActuationClosed/PostconditionObserved/ReceiptEmitted events carrying pre/post-state digests. Real code, present on disk and used by receipt emission paths; unit tests exist for the chain/verify layer (PI1-1/PI1-2) but not a dedicated test asserting OCEL log completeness/accuracy itself, hence IMPLEMENTED rather than TESTED for this specific record-keeping criterion." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Storage of inputs/outputs/data throughout processing is complete, accurate, timely, authorized (storage integrity)" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-5" ;
    dcterms:type "TESTED" ;
    dcterms:contributor "chatman-ecosystem" ;
    dcterms:source "platform-console/services/ggen/ggen-src/crates/ggen-config/src/receipt/receipt_impl.rs:27-156 (Receipt::sign/verify/hash/chain); crates/ggen-config/src/receipt/chain.rs:274-301 (test_chain_verify); crates/ggen-engine/src/keys.rs:404-424,761-794" ;
    dcterms:description "Receipt is Ed25519-signed and SHA-256-hashed (with a separate BLAKE3-hashed ReceiptRecord type coexisting) with an unbroken previous-hash chain; ReceiptChain::verify() is exercised by a real passing test that signs a 3-receipt chain and confirms tamper-free verification. keys.rs's resolve_signing_key persists an ed25519 signing key to disk restricted to 0600 owner-only permissions, confirmed by a real passing test reading back the file mode. A real passing test (receipt_tampering_is_detected) mutates a signed field and asserts verification then fails -- direct evidence storage integrity (tamper-detection) actually works, not just exists." .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exceptions -> prov:Entity (dcterms:type "EXCEPTION")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Single control-plane node, no HA/failover -- disclosed, unmitigated availability risk" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC9-1" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "HIGH" ;
    dcterms:description "docs/SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md #1 and SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md 'Still Open' both state the cluster runs one etcd, one API server, one kubelet, and has already suffered one unrecoverable etcd bbolt corruption requiring full manual recreation. This is a verifiably real, currently-open gap, not remediated in this checkout." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Stand up a multi-node control plane (or managed control plane) with etcd HA before any production/customer commitment is made against this platform." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Single-Pod Postgres per project, no streaming replica, no continuous point-in-time recovery" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "HIGH" ;
    dcterms:description "SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md 'Still Open' -> PaaS section: only on-demand pg_dump snapshots exist; the same doc discloses a real observed restore defect where FK-order-dependent rows can land unrestored." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Add a streaming replica/standby and continuous WAL-based PITR; fix the documented FK-order restore defect and re-verify with a real restore test." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "etcd secret-encryption key stored on same node disk as the ciphertext" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC3" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md item 1 explicitly discloses that the aescbc encryption key lives on the same node's disk as etcd, so it defends against etcd-data-exfiltration and backup theft but not full node compromise (root-on-node can read the key next to the ciphertext); also scoped to Secrets only, ConfigMaps remain plaintext." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Move to a remote KMS-backed envelope provider once an external KMS is available to the cluster; extend encryption coverage to ConfigMaps holding sensitive data." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Audit log lives in the same Postgres cluster it audits (not physically isolated)" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC7" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "SONY-READINESS-GAP-CLOSURE.md item 4 states plainly this is 'the hash-chain alternative the survey gap explicitly named, not the stronger option (isolated/separate audit sink)' -- a row can no longer be silently rewritten undetected, but the store itself is not physically separate from the system it audits." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Ship audit log rows to a separate, append-only sink (e.g. a WORM object store or separate audited database) in addition to the in-place hash chain." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "RBAC patch-verb gap on custom-domain TLS Secrets (found and fixed)" ;
    dcterms:subject "CC6" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "LOW" ;
    dcterms:description "platform-console/README.md (~line 101, custom-domains-tls RBAC gap) documents that the first live certificate-rotation attempt failed with a real 'secrets ... is forbidden ... cannot patch resource' error because platform-console-custom-domains-tls Role (k8s/paas-rbac.yaml) granted get/list/create/delete but not patch on istio-system Secrets. This was a real, disclosed, already-fixed gap (verb added), not a currently-open exception, but is named here per the task's request to identify RBAC-permission gaps of this kind." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Already remediated in-repo: patch verb added to platform-console-custom-domains-tls Role in k8s/paas-rbac.yaml; live-verified via a successful zero-downtime rotation afterward." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "No documented contractual SLA or availability commitment" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "docs/SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md section 4 explicitly states the platform makes 'no promise about future uptime' and 'offers no remedy for downtime.' If A1.1 requires an actual availability commitment (not just monitoring), this system has none, and the gap is honestly self-documented rather than hidden." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Not applicable to a lab/demo single-node kind cluster per the repo's own stated scope; would require a real SLA document and a production multi-node control plane before this criterion could move past NOT-STARTED." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Single control-plane node, no HA/failover" ;
    dcterms:subject "A1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "HIGH" ;
    dcterms:description "docs/SCOPE-AND-LIMITATIONS.md section 1 states this is a single-node kind cluster with no etcd quorum, no second API server, no kubelet failover -- if the one node dies, every workload in every namespace goes down simultaneously with no automatic recovery, as already happened once (the incident documented in DISASTER-RECOVERY.md)." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Documented as an inherent, disclosed limitation of the current lab environment; would require a real multi-node/multi-AZ control plane to remediate." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Signing key not durable across pod rescheduling (no PVC)" ;
    dcterms:subject "C1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "services/ggen/app.py:48-52 states plainly that when no GGEN_SIGNING_KEY is operator-injected, the locally generated signing key at SIGNING_KEY_PATH (default /app/state/keys/signing.key) is only as durable as the pod's local storage -- no PersistentVolumeClaim exists for this Deployment today, so a pod reschedule generates a fresh key and receipts signed under the old key can no longer be verified. This is a real, currently-true gap disclosed in-repo, not remediated." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Wire a PVC for the key path, or source the key exclusively from a k8s Secret set up out-of-band (per the same comment's own stated recommendation)." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "No data classification scheme exists" ;
    dcterms:subject "C1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "C1.1 has zero control coverage in the SOC2 mapping doc and no supporting policy/code anywhere in the repo -- confirmed absent, not merely undocumented in the mapping." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Author a data-classification policy identifying sensitivity tiers for the data types this platform actually handles (k8s Secrets, signing keys, project metadata) and map existing protection controls to it." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "Signing key is filesystem-persisted with process-local generation-on-first-use, not centrally managed KMS-backed key material for most components" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-1" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "ggen-engine/src/keys.rs and platform-console/services/ggen/app.py's resolve_signing_key() both generate and persist a fresh ed25519/hex signing key to a local file (.ggen/keys/signing.key or SIGNING_KEY_PATH) on first use if no GGEN_SIGNING_KEY env var is present, with correct 0600 permissions -- but this is per-process/per-node local key material, not a k8s Secret/KMS-backed key by default; the env var precedence exists but nothing in the code enforces that operators actually inject a Secret-backed key in production, so a pod restart without a persistent volume for .ggen/keys silently mints a new signing identity and breaks receipt-chain continuity across restarts." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Mount .ggen/keys (or SIGNING_KEY_PATH) on a PVC or require GGEN_SIGNING_KEY to be sourced from a k8s Secret in all production deployment manifests, and add a startup check that refuses to silently regenerate a signing key when one is expected to already exist." .

[] a prov:Entity ;
    rdfs:label "SPARQL injection detection is a keyword blocklist, not a parser-level allowlist" ;
    dcterms:subject "PI1-2" ;
    dcterms:type "EXCEPTION" ;
    dcterms:relation "MEDIUM" ;
    dcterms:description "ggen-graph/src/interchangeable.rs's admit_input() and ggen-marketplace/src/marketplace/rdf/rdf_control.rs's execute_query() both rely on substring/pattern detection of specific dangerous SPARQL constructs (DROP GRAPH / DELETE WHERE, admit_input, plus a separate FMEA-tracked 'detect_injection' scanner) rather than a strict query-shape allowlist (e.g. ASK/SELECT-only), leaving a structural gap for as-yet-unenumerated destructive SPARQL Update forms." ;
    dcterms:isReplacedBy "Constrain admitted queries to a parsed allowlist of query forms (ASK/SELECT/CONSTRUCT) at the graph engine boundary rather than blocklisting known-bad substrings." .

